  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "+BVyQvUITAbzrZjfzuL8ccdEkFw=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T08:45:55.525Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "`addons/l10n_de/models/res_company.py` contains `company.force_restrictive_audit_trail |= company.country_code == 'DE'`, and `addons/account/models/company.py` enforces it: attempting to disable raises *\"Can't disable restricted audit trail: forced by localization.\"*\n\nThe German fiscal documentation states that *\"Odoo is certified GoBD-compliant\"* and that with the German localization *\"Odoo is in standard configured in such a way that the inalterability clause can be adhered to without any further customization.\"* A SHA-256 hash chain over eight accounting fields backs it, each entry incorporating the previous entry's hash.\n\nFor a German buyer this makes Odoo the statutory books rather than a candidate for replacement. An external record layer should not attempt to be a parallel ledger here; the honest role is integration.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-20T08:45:55.525348Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T08:45:55.525352Z"
    }
  },
